clean_summary:
I’ve known and respected @skairam's work for years. The thoughtfulness and rigor he brings to building and evaluating complex models are truly rare. Thrilled that we are now colleagues at @simile_ai.

Welcome to the team, Sanjay!

@skairam: "After an extraordinary chapter at @OpenAI, I’ve joined @simile_ai to define what rigorous evals look like for AI systems that simulate human behavior. It’s one of those rare roles where a strange collection of career obsessions suddenly belongs in the same room."

We don’t care for superintelligent, rational models. Instead, we are building models that represent our tastes, values, and behaviors. Do this right, and we have a representation of humanity at scale.

@skairam is awesome, and we are building a killer eval team at @simile_ai. Join us!

@skairam: "I’m one month into @SimileAI, and I’m even more convinced that evals for simulating human behavior is one of the most interesting problems in AI. That's why we’re growing our small-but-mighty Evals team by hiring multiple Evals -- MTS roles in SF + NYC."

The first time I read @joon_s_pk and team’s paper on generative agents, I was a student in @msbernst’s class. I was so in awe of their work, and a future where we could simulate what previously felt unsimulate-able, that I sent it to almost everyone I knew.

Major congrats to team @simile_ai. The world is a better place when this level of brilliance comes together to work on something that was once supposed to be limited to science fiction. Go team!

@joon_s_pk: "Five months ago, we launched @simile_ai with the belief that simulation would become a new way for the world to make decisions. Today, that belief feels less like a thesis and more like the beginning of a new category. Incredibly proud of my team. We are just getting started."
